#
# Conformance case: coreference/counterpart-not-transitive
#
# AC: gmeow:counterpartOf is symmetric-only by design and must NEVER be derived —
# in particular it must not chain transitively. The standing
# logic:CounterpartNonTransitivityObligation forbids any rule head from producing
# gmeow:counterpartOf (Arm A syntactic reachability), enforced over the whole reasoned
# graph by `make verify`; this case is its adversarial complement at the engine level.
#
# input.nq models a genuine two-hop counterpart chain as DATA: a gmeow:counterpartOf b
# and b gmeow:counterpartOf c, across realms. If counterpart were transitive, a chase
# would derive a gmeow:counterpartOf c — collapsing two distinct cross-realm links into a
# transitively-identified one. It does not: no rule head produces gmeow:counterpartOf.
#
# This program ships a POSITIVE CONTROL — a monotone Horn rule that DOES fire on the
# counterpart edges (counterpartOf(x,y) ⇒ ex:counterpartWitnessed(x,y)), so the chase is
# provably live and actively reasons over the counterpart structure. That the live chase
# still derives NO gmeow:counterpartOf(a,c) is thus a meaningful observation, not the side
# effect of an empty run: materialized.nq is a strict superset of input.nq carrying the
# ex:counterpartWitnessed edges and NO transitive counterpart edge.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/coreference/counterpart-not-transitive/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# ── Positive control — a monotone Horn rule anchored to the counterpart edges ──
# counterpartOf(x,y) ⇒ ex:counterpartWitnessed(x,y)
# Its head is an ex: predicate nowhere near gmeow:counterpartOf, so the guardrail is
# untouched; the chase DOES derive it (materialized ⊋ input), proving the engine reasons
# over the counterpart structure while deriving no transitive counterpart edge.
ex:ruleCounterpartWitness
    a logic:Rule ;
    logic:provenance ex:ruleCounterpartWitness ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?x" ;
        rdf:predicate ex:counterpartWitnessed ;
        rdf:object    "?y"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?x" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:counterpartOf ;
        rdf:object    "?y"
    ] .
